<%# Port of `Hujah/form.js` displayParentCard: reminds the replier how they voted on
    the parent, then shows the parent body with a stance-colored left border.
    Locals: parent.

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.3) — this is the third surface that reaches for the
    8px stance border, and `DesignSystemHelper::CARD_STANCES` names it explicitly:
    "`hujahs/_parent_card` falls back to `primary` when the viewer never voted". So the
    body block goes through `ui/_card` with `stance:` instead of interpolating
    `border-<...>` by hand — same reason as `_child_card`: the helper raises on a value
    outside the set, raw interpolation renders a borderless card and says nothing.

    That DOES change one pixel-level thing: `ui/_card` carries `shadow`, and this block
    had `bg-white` alone. It is a card in every other respect — white, square, stance
    border — and the design system has one card surface, not two. Treat the shadow as
    the correction it is, the same way `ui/_empty_state` adds `bg-white` to the three
    call sites that had no background.

    `padded:` stays unset so `pl-2` in `class:` cannot collide with it (the same-family
    padding trap in ui/_card's header).

    The stance verb above the card keeps its raw `text-<stance> fill-<stance>`
    interpolation. Both are BARE utilities over the stance trio, which
    `@source inline("{bg,text,border,fill}-{agree,neutral,disagree,primary}")` covers —
    unlike a variant such as `peer-checked:bg-<stance>`, which a safelist entry does not
    generate and which shipped blank in `_stance_picker` until Task 4.2. `stance` here is
    nil or one of the trio; `verb` gates the span, so nothing renders when it is nil. %>
<%
  stance = parent.current_user_vote(logged_in: true, current_user_id: current_user.id)
  verb = {"agree" => "agreed", "neutral" => "were neutral", "disagree" => "disagreed"}[stance]
%>
<div class="bg-white pb-2">
  <small class="text-sm text-grey">
    You
    <% if verb %>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-<%= stance %> fill-<%= stance %>">
        <%= stance_icon(stance, class: "w-4 h-4") %><%= verb %>
      </span>
    <% end %>
    to <span class="text-primary"><%= parent.user.full_name %></span>'s claim:
  </small>
</div>
<%= render layout: "ui/card", locals: {stance: stance || "primary", class: "pl-2"} do %>
  <h6 class="text-black pt-1 leading-snug"><%= format_body(parent.body) %></h6>
<% end %>
